From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Bright <william.bright@imd-tec.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 11:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] misc: fastrpc: retry INIT_CREATE on transient DSP teardown
 race

client_id (session slot) reuse can race the async tail of the DSP's
own teardown for the previous occupant of that same slot:
fastrpc_device_release() blocks until the DSP acks
FASTRPC_RMID_INIT_RELEASE, but internal cleanup on the DSP side for
that client_id can still be finishing when a new process is handed
the same slot moments later by fastrpc_session_alloc().

Observed on QCS8550 cdsp: back-to-back FASTRPC_IOCTL_INIT_CREATE
calls (fresh open()/close() per call, unsigned PD) intermittently
fail with AEE_ERESOURCENOTFOUND (0x80000416) or AEE_EALREADY
(0x8000041a) even though the same call reliably succeeds when spaced
out by a second, or on a second attempt moments later. This is a
timing race, not a real rejection.

Retry the INIT_CREATE invoke a bounded number of times with a short
backoff when the DSP returns one of these two specific transient
statuses, before giving up and returning the error to userspace as
before.

Signed-off-by: William Bright <william.bright@imd-tec.com>
---
 drivers/misc/fastrpc.c | 33 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 29 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c b/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c
--- a/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c
@@ -27,6 +27,7 @@
 #include <linux/bitops.h>
 #include <linux/compiler.h>
 #include <linux/iopoll.h>
+#include <linux/delay.h>

 #define ADSP_DOMAIN_ID (0)
 #define MDSP_DOMAIN_ID (1)
@@ -108,6 +109,15 @@
 #define FASTRPC_RMID_INIT_MEM_MAP      10
 #define FASTRPC_RMID_INIT_MEM_UNMAP    11

+/*
+ * DSP-side statuses (AEEStdErr.h) seen transiently when a create races the
+ * async tail of a just-completed release for the same client_id/PID slot.
+ */
+#define AEE_ERESOURCENOTFOUND		0x80000416
+#define AEE_EALREADY			0x8000041a
+#define FASTRPC_INIT_CREATE_RETRIES	10
+#define FASTRPC_INIT_CREATE_RETRY_DELAY_MS	5
+
 /* Protection Domain(PD) ids */
 #define ROOT_PD		(0)
 #define USER_PD		(1)
@@ -1759,8 +1769,23 @@
 	if (init.attrs)
 		sc = FASTRPC_SCALARS(FASTRPC_RMID_INIT_CREATE_ATTR, 4, 0);

-	err = fastrpc_internal_invoke(fl, true, FASTRPC_INIT_HANDLE,
-				      sc, args);
+	{
+		int attempt;
+
+		for (attempt = 0; attempt < FASTRPC_INIT_CREATE_RETRIES; attempt++) {
+			err = fastrpc_internal_invoke(fl, true, FASTRPC_INIT_HANDLE,
+						      sc, args);
+			if (err != AEE_ERESOURCENOTFOUND && err != AEE_EALREADY)
+				break;
+			/*
+			 * The client_id slot we were just handed can still be
+			 * finishing async DSP-side teardown from its previous
+			 * occupant's release. Back off briefly and retry rather
+			 * than failing a legitimate create.
+			 */
+			msleep(FASTRPC_INIT_CREATE_RETRY_DELAY_MS);
+		}
+	}
 	if (err)
 		goto err_invoke;

--
2.41.0
